WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:01.734
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:02.868
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.834
You're here. You're watching.
Thank you.

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:06.634
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.033
Well, guys, everyone's excited
about this --

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.601
the 95th Oscars are this Sunday.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.367
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]
Yeah.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:15.400
I love the Oscars
because it's the one time

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.133
we get to make James Cameron sit
in a theater for five hours.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:22.634
Ten movies are nominated
for Best Picture,

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:25.801
including "Top Gun: Maverick,"
"Avatar" 2, "Elvis,"

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.934
and seven other films
that you lied about seeing.

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:32.634
This will be Jimmy Kimmel's
third time hosting the Oscars.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:36.000
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.434
Which means it will also be
the third time

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:39.567
my dad calls the next day like,

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:41.367
"You did a great job
hosting the Oscars.

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:45.267
You got funny all of a sudden,
huh?"

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:48.734
[ Laughter ]
That's right, the Oscars
are finally here.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.167
For everyone nominated,
just remember --

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:51.434
even if you don't win,

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.033
Fox News might say you did.

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:54.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:57.067
[ Ohhs and cheering ]

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:58.734
[ Rimshot ]
-Preach!

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.367
[ Whistling and applause ]

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:03.000
-Well, as you probably heard,
the White House and Congress

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.767
are talking
about banning TikTok.

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:05.934
[ Oohs ]

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.734
They're worried about China
spying on us,

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.534
so, it might be outlawed.

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:11.133
Yeah, so, they're trying
to take it down,

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:13.100
but I have a feeling
it might stay put.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:13.801
Kind of like --

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:15.400
[ Cheering ]

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.467
[ Ohhs and laughter ]

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:19.934
I mean, people
really love TikTok.

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:21.968
It'd be hard to watch it go
down in flames.

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:22.634
Sort of like --

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:24.367
Whee-un!

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:25.467
[ Ohhs ]

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:26.367
Whee--

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:27.834
[ Screaming ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:29.300
-It raises --

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.634
It raises so many questions.

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:32.701
Will TikTok be totally gone

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:33.868
or will parts of it remain?

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:34.534
Kind of like --

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:36.567
-Oh, no!

00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:37.801
[ Ohhs ]

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:39.400
[ Screaming and applause ]

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:42.601
Or like --

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:45.100
[ Sighs ]

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.667
[ Ohhs ]

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:50.133
[ Laughter ]
Either way,

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.801
you can feel the tension
getting high, almost like --

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:56.400
[ Clattering ]
[ Ohhs ]

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.934
-Olivia, you [bleep] idiot!

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:01.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:01.834
Long --
[ Laughs ]

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:05.200
Long story short,
if TikTok is outlawed,

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.667
it'll leave a giant hole
in our hearts.

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:07.334
Kind of like --

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:11.834
[ Gasps ]
[ Ohhs ]

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:13.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:13.901
My favorite.

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:21.167
-What?
-His head just went
through the wall, yeah.

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:22.701
It's the best.

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:24.968
Some more political news --
it sounds like

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:26.534
former President Trump
will likely

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:29.434
face criminal charges
for his hush money payments

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:30.834
to Stormy Daniels.

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:32.734
[ Oohs ]
Trump was like --

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:35.133
[ As Trump ]
I've never regretted
30 seconds more in my life.

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:38.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.033
Right now,
Democrats are thinking,

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:42.400
"Wow, it's like we're getting
two Oscars in one week."

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.267
[ Laughter and applause ]
Switching gears --
I saw that South Korea

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:48.267
is building the world's biggest
spokeless Ferris wheel.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.234
[ Oohs ]
Can we see a photo?
Look at this.

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:51.767
Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:53.767
It looks like God's aura ring.

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:55.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:56.734
You actually have one of those
aura rings, don't you?

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:57.968
-Yeah, I did.
-You don't like it?

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.267
-I didn't care for at all.
-Why?

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:02.901
-Always said I was asleep
and it hurt so bad to put it on.

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:04.000
It hurt really bad.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:06.901
-What finger do you have it on?

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:11.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.167
-Never mind.
-Supposed to go --

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:15.834
Just cut away,
cut away from me, cut away.

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:16.667
We can cut this out.

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:19.100
Ohhh!

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.000
-God.
Terrible.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.033
-You're supposed to put it
on your finger?

00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:24.767
-You got to read --

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:27.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:28.334
-Now, it makes sense.
-Read the instructions.

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:29.634
-Yeah.
-You have to read
the instructions.

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:31.501
-Ouch!
-You just went
with your instinct on it.

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:32.701
-Yeah. Figured, why not?
-Yeah.

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:35.033
No, no, no, no.
-Oof!

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:38.133
-Well, this is going viral --
supermarket chain Aldi

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:40.634
has new Easter bunny
marshmallow snacks,

00:03:40.634 --> 00:03:41.701
but some people have noticed

00:03:41.701 --> 00:03:44.167
they don't really look
like bunnies.

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:45.334
Check this out here.

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:48.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.167
Even worse, they slapped on
a warning label that says,

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.467
"May contain nuts."
-Oh, hey!

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.234
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:56.234 --> 00:03:58.534
It's the only Easter candy
that's perfect for Easter

00:03:58.534 --> 00:04:00.367
and a bachelorette party.
-Oh!

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:02.534
[ Laughter and applause ]
You should put an aura
ring on it.

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:03.734
-Yeah.

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:04.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:06.167
Don't put it on those.

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:07.634
-♪ If you want it, you gotta
put an aura ring on it ♪

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:08.701
-Finally...

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:10.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:12.701
...a burglar in the UK
was identified

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:15.868
after leaving his birth
certificate at a crime scene.

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:16.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:18.133
Forget leaving it
at a crime scene.

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:19.601
Who walks around with their
birth certificate?

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:21.701
[ Laughter ]
Right now, police are
on the lookout

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:23.901
for a man who weighs
7 pounds, 3 ounces.

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:25.200
[ Laughter and applause ]
We have a great show.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.367
Let's go write
some thank you notes.

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:27.601
Come on with me.
Come on.

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:29.334
-♪ JKLMNOP ♪

00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:31.234
♪ [ Indistinct ] ♪

00:04:31.234 --> 00:04:32.200
♪ But freeze ♪

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.634
♪ Catch the wave, later ♪

00:04:33.634 --> 00:04:35.501
♪ That was like the alphabet,
but I'm an Alpha Beta ♪

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:37.267
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:38.667
-What a show!

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:41.400
What a show we have
for you tonight.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:44.701
She stars in the new movie
"Shazam! Fury of the Gods,"

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:48.000
which opens in theaters
and IMAX March 17th.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.834
Our pal Lucy Liu
is here tonight!
-Yeah!

00:04:50.834 --> 00:04:53.434
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:53.434 --> 00:04:55.033
-I love Lucy Liu.
-Yeah.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.534
You can see him
in the FX series "Snowfall,"

00:04:58.534 --> 00:04:59.801
which airs Wednesdays

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:01.834
and streams the next day
on Hulu.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:04.000
Damson Idris is joining us!
-Yeah!

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.501
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Stud.

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:09.400
Studly show.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.801
Plus, we've got some great,
great, great music.

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:15.434
He's a five-time
Latin Grammy-nominated producer

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:20.100
and she is the best-selling
female Latin artist of all time.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.501
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Oh!
-All time!

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:25.167
-♪ Shakira, Shakira ♪
-Their new song,

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:28.000
"music sessions vol. 53"
is out now.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.767
and breaking records everywhere.

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:33.167
Music superstars Bizarrap
and Shakira

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:34.767
-Oh!
-are here tonight!

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:37.701
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:38.734
-Come on!

00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:40.000
-We're going to talk to them

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.801
and they're performing for us
later in the show.

00:05:41.801 --> 00:05:42.968
-Oy!
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:46.601
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:46.601 --> 00:05:48.167
Guys, today is Friday
and that's usually

00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:49.634
when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:51.701
I check my inbox,
return some emails,

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:53.400
and, of course, I send out
thank you notes.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.067
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:55.067 --> 00:05:56.834
I was running a bit behind.

00:05:56.834 --> 00:05:58.734
I was wondering, can I write out
some thank you notes right now?

00:05:58.734 --> 00:05:59.767
Is that okay with you guys?

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:00.868
[ Cheering and applause ]
I appreciate it.

00:06:03.033 --> 00:06:05.234
James, can I get some thank you
note writing music, please?

00:06:05.234 --> 00:06:06.667
[ Playing tender tune ]

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:09.667
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:12.868
♪♪

00:06:12.868 --> 00:06:14.000
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:17.200
Thank you,
Daylight Savings this Sunday,

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.067
for kicking off
that special half of the year

00:06:19.067 --> 00:06:21.467
when our microwaves are actually
set to the right time.

00:06:21.467 --> 00:06:22.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:24.934
-Hey, yeah!

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:26.133
-I knew it!
-Oh!

00:06:28.267 --> 00:06:29.601
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.601 --> 00:06:31.167
-Thank you, Apple,

00:06:31.167 --> 00:06:33.033
